# haiku-repo-coherence.baseline -- EXACT (`==`) requirements that a live DeBeOS
# pool already cannot satisfy (issue 708).
#
# These are pre-existing debt, not accepted design. Each line is a package that
# is UNINSTALLABLE right now. They are listed so that the coherence gate blocks
# NEW incoherence without blocking every unrelated publish; clearing one means
# rebuilding and republishing the port, after which `--strict-baseline` reports
# the line as STALE and it must be deleted. The list only shrinks.
#
# Format:  <pinning-package> <required-resolvable> <required-version>   # reason
# (the key is the first three fields; everything after `#` is the reason)
#
# ONE FILE, EVERY TARGET. The gate runs over the union of whatever pool is being
# published into plus the incoming set, so a baseline cut against ONE target
# blocks the others on debt they did not create (issue 852: this file was
# measured against green, and every blue publish then failed on blue's own
# bootstrap-era orphans). A key is a package's broken pin, which is a fact about
# the package and not about where it is stored, so the entries are pooled here
# and each section says where it was measured.
#
# Measured against:
#   - s3://<pool>/debeos-repo-green/arm64/repo of 2026-10-14   (green)
#   - s3://<pool>/debeos-repo/arm64/packages/ of 2026-10-19    (blue, issue 852)
#   - s3://<work>/hpkg/arm64/ of 2026-10-19                    (wave harvest, issue 852)

# --- base superseded out from under a subpackage (the issue-708 defect) ------
# haiku-repo-add's per-NAME supersede dropped the pinned base version; the
# subpackage is a different name, so the glob left it behind. Fix: rebuild and
# republish the subpackage at the base's current version.
ripgrep_debuginfo ripgrep 14.0.1      # base at 15.2.0-1; debuginfo never rebuilt

# --- base never published for arm64 at all -----------------------------------
# The arch-independent subpackage was published while its arch-specific base
# was not, so there is nothing to pin to. Fix: build the base for arm64, or drop
# the orphaned subpackage from the pool.
moleinvasion_music moleinvasion 0.4   # no moleinvasion-* in the arm64 pool

# --- resolvable never packaged for arm64 -------------------------------------
# No Java runtime is ported to Haiku arm64, so nothing can provide java:runtime.
# geogebra is unusable on this arch regardless of the repo's coherence.
geogebra java:runtime 8               # no JRE port for arm64

# --- blue: subpackage published against a BOOTSTRAP base (issue 852) ---------
# Blue (`debeos-repo/arm64`) was seeded on 2026-09-21 from a bootstrap set: the
# base is the `_bootstrap` build at an older version, while a later non-bootstrap
# subpackage was published beside it, pinning a version blue never carried. These
# predate every build wave, so they are not a wave's incoherence to answer for.
# Fix: build and publish the non-bootstrap base at the pinned version (which
# retires the `_bootstrap` package too), then delete the line.
coreutils_debuginfo coreutils 9.11    # blue has coreutils-9.9_bootstrap-1 only
freetype_debuginfo freetype 2.14.3    # blue has freetype-2.6.3_bootstrap-1 only

# --- subpackage pins the WRONG resolvable name (issue 852) -------------------
# icu67_tools requires the generic `icu == 67.1`, but the package that carries
# 67.1 is named icu67 and provides only `icu67` (verified by reading
# icu67-67.1-1-arm64.hpkg: provides icu67, lib:libicu*, never `icu`). The only
# `icu` in blue is icu-57.2-3. So no publish of any icu can satisfy this pin --
# it is a recipe defect in the icu67 port's `_tools` subpackage, not missing
# build output. Fix: correct the recipe's REQUIRES to icu67, rebuild, republish.
icu67_tools icu 67.1                  # pins `icu`, but 67.1 is provided as `icu67`

# --- harvest: subpackage built and harvested without its base (issue 852) ----
# The wave harvest holds a `_devel` whose base was never harvested alongside it,
# so the incoming set offers the subpackage alone. Published as accepted debt on
# the operator's call (2026-10-20) rather than held back, so the rest of the
# wave output is not blocked behind them. Fix: build the base at the pinned
# version and publish the pair, then delete the line.
ffmpeg7_devel ffmpeg7 7.1             # no ffmpeg7 base in blue or the harvest
icu78_devel icu78 78.3                # no icu78 base in blue or the harvest
